From: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 10:30:00 +0800
Subject: Fix absolute symlink handling on Linux

7-Zip incorrectly strips the leading '/' from absolute symlink
targets on Linux (e.g. /opt/deepin-wine11-stable/lib/...), then
prepends the extraction output directory, producing broken symlinks
like /tmp/extract/opt/deepin-... instead of /opt/deepin-...

Root cause: CLinkInfo::Remove_AbsPathPrefixes() unconditionally
removes the root prefix '/' from absolute paths, treating them as
relative to the archive root. The subsequent SetLink2() then
prepends the extraction directory, producing incorrect paths.

Fix:
1. In Remove_AbsPathPrefixes(): on Linux, preserve absolute
   symlink paths starting with '/' instead of stripping the prefix.
2. In SetLink2() security check: allow Linux absolute paths
   (non-Windows absolute paths) through the IsAbsolute check.
3. In SetLink2() IsSafePath check: skip the safety check for
   Linux absolute paths since they are valid absolute paths.

Signed-off-by: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
---
--- 7zip.orig/CPP/7zip/UI/Common/ArchiveExtractCallback.cpp
+++ 7zip/CPP/7zip/UI/Common/ArchiveExtractCallback.cpp
@@ -2171,8 +2171,13 @@ static HRESULT SetLink2(const CArchiveExtractCallback &callback,
     li.Parse(link.LinkPath, link.Is_WSL());
     bool isDang;
     UString relativePathPrefix;
-    if (li.IsAbsolute // unexpected
-        || li.ParentDirDots_after_NonParent
+    if ((li.IsAbsolute // unexpected
+#ifndef _WIN32
+        // On Linux, absolute symlinks (e.g., /opt/...) are valid and should
+        // be preserved. Only reject Windows-style absolute paths.
+        && link.isWindowsPath
+#endif
+        ) || li.ParentDirDots_after_NonParent
         || (level <= 5 && link.isRelative && li.FinalLevel < 1) // final level lower
         || (level <= 5 && link.isRelative && li.LowLevel < 0)   // negative temporary levels
        )
@@ -2204,8 +2209,16 @@ static HRESULT SetLink2(const CArchiveExtractCallback &callback,
       if (!link.isRelative), then (path == link.LinkPath)
       */
       isDang = false;
+#ifndef _WIN32
+      // On Linux, absolute symlink paths (starting with '/') are valid.
+      // Skip IsSafePath for absolute paths; use it for relative paths.
+      if (!(path[0] == WCHAR_PATH_SEPARATOR && !link.isRelative)
+          && !IsSafePath(path, link.Is_WSL()))
+        isDang = true;
+#else
       if (!IsSafePath(path, link.Is_WSL()))
         isDang = true;
+#endif
     }
     const char *message = NULL;
     if (isDang)
@@ -2431,6 +2444,19 @@ void CLinkInfo::Remove_AbsPathPrefixes()
         break;
       n = 1;
     }
+
+#ifndef _WIN32
+    // On Linux, preserve absolute symlink paths (starting with '/')
+    // as they are valid absolute paths in the filesystem.
+    // Do NOT strip the leading '/' to avoid the path being reinterpreted
+    // as relative to the extraction output directory.
+    if (!isWindowsPath)
+    {
+      isRelative = false;
+      return;
+    }
+#endif
+
     isRelative = false; // (LinkPath) will be treated as relative to root folder of archive
     LinkPath.DeleteFrontal(n);
   }

